## Prompt Engineering: Better Results Ke Liye Practical Rules

Vibe coding mein prompt quality important hai, lekin long prompt hamesha better prompt nahi hota. Clear, testable aur scoped requirements generally zyada useful hoti hain.

### Rule 1: User Aur Problem Clearly Define Karein

Weak prompt:

```text
Make a great productivity app.
```

Better prompt:

```text
Build a simple productivity app for college students who want to track
assignments and due dates. The first version should allow users to add,
complete, and delete assignments. Keep the interface mobile-friendly.
Do not add login or cloud synchronisation in this version.
```

### Rule 2: Requirements Ko Acceptance Criteria Mein Convert Karein

Acceptance criteria woh conditions hain jinse aap determine kar sakte hain ki feature actually work karta hai ya nahi.

Example:

- User empty task submit nahi kar sakta.
- Task complete mark karne par visual state update hoti hai.
- Refresh ke baad saved tasks load hote hain.
- Delete action sirf selected task ko remove karta hai.

Aise criteria vague statements jaise “app properly work karni chahiye” se zyada useful hain.

### Rule 3: AI Ko Ek Time Par Ek Major Change Dein

Agar aap ek hi prompt mein design, database, authentication, analytics aur deployment modify karwa denge, toh errors ka source identify karna difficult ho sakta hai.

Features ko phases mein divide karein:

1. Core interface.
2. Basic interactions.
3. Data persistence.
4. Validation and error handling.
5. Tests and accessibility.
6. Deployment.

### Rule 4: AI Se Trade-Offs Explain Karwayein

Agar AI ek new dependency add kar raha hai, toh usse poochhein ki dependency kyon necessary hai, alternatives kya hain aur maintenance implications kya ho sakte hain.

AI ka answer final authority nahi hai, lekin trade-offs explain karwana aapko better decision lene mein help karta hai.

### Rule 5: Tests Aur Documentation Ko Workflow Ka Part Banayein

Sirf code generate karwana enough nahi. AI se tests draft karwa sakte hain, edge cases identify karwa sakte hain aur README documentation banwa sakte hain.

Lekin generated tests ko bhi review karein. Agar test incorrect behaviour ko expected result maan leta hai, toh green test suite ke bawajood application wrong ho sakti hai.

