## Security, Privacy Aur Responsible AI Coding

Vibe coding ke excitement mein security fundamentals ignore karna easy hai. Lekin generated code bhi ordinary software ki tarah vulnerabilities introduce kar sakta hai.

### API Keys Aur Secrets Protect Karein

Private API keys, passwords aur access tokens ko frontend code ya public repository mein hardcode nahi karna chahiye.

Server-side secrets ko appropriate environment configuration ya secret-management system mein rakhein. Agar koi key accidentally expose ho jaaye, toh usse revoke ya rotate karein.

### Authentication Aur Authorisation Ko Alag Samjhein

Authentication ka matlab hai user kaun hai, yeh verify karna. Authorisation decide karta hai ki user ko kaun-se resources access karne ki permission hai.

Sirf login screen generate kar dena secure access control ka proof nahi hai. Backend ko har sensitive request par permissions enforce karni chahiye.

### User Data Ko Carefully Handle Karein

Agar application names, phone numbers, financial information ya other personal data process karti hai, toh minimum necessary data collect karein.

AI tool mein proprietary code ya sensitive records paste karne se pehle applicable privacy settings, organisational policies aur data-handling terms check karein.

### Dependencies Aur Generated Commands Review Karein

Unknown scripts, package installation commands aur generated shell commands ko samjhe bina execute mat karein. Untrusted code environment files, project files ya external resources access kar sakta hai.

### AI-Generated Code Ko Test Karein

Security review mein relevant areas include kar sakte hain:

- Input validation.
- Access control.
- Database queries aur data handling.
- Authentication flows.
- File uploads.
- Dependency vulnerabilities.
- Error messages aur logging.
- Secret exposure.

Application ki risk level ke according appropriate automated scanning aur qualified human review arrange karein. Financial, healthcare ya other regulated use cases mein applicable legal, privacy aur compliance obligations separately assess karna zaroori hai.

